      ":question/id": "ce69fac0-2ef1-5e13-8bff-0a6a8d0e1838",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/52/52f6354e4d078a913170461a9b0435f0d3f8b5bace314e27c12235d85331aa9c.png)\n\nIn the diagram, $Q$ lies on the segment $PT$. The given vectors are $\\overrightarrow{OP}=w$ and $\\overrightarrow{OT}=n$. The lengths satisfy $PQ:QT=1:1$.\n\nExpress $\\overrightarrow{OQ}$ in terms of $w$ and $n$. Fill in both coefficients, including their signs.\n\n$\\overrightarrow{OQ}=$ {{field-1}} $w+$ {{field-2}} $n$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First express both endpoint vectors in the directions away from $O$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{OP}=w\\qquad \\overrightarrow{OT}=n .\n$$\n\nTrace the path from $P$ through $O$ to $T$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{PT}=\\overrightarrow{PO}+\\overrightarrow{OT}=-w+n.\n$$\n\nThe ratio $PQ:QT=1:1$ gives $2$ parts in the whole segment. Thus\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{PQ}=\\frac{1}{2}\\overrightarrow{PT}=\\frac{1}{2}(-w+n).\n$$\n\nAdd along the path $O\\to P\\to Q$ and collect coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overrightarrow{OQ}&=\\overrightarrow{OP}+\\overrightarrow{PQ}\\\\&=w+\\frac{1}{2}(-w+n)\\\\&=\\frac{1}{2}w+\\frac{1}{2}n.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
