      ":question/problem": "![](images/83/83eb44871943dc3b4f32c2ddd9629958ed9632267ccf2176885ef4f535c9d7e8.png)\n\nIn the diagram, $D$ lies on the segment $EL$. The given vectors are $\\overrightarrow{OE}=p$ and $\\overrightarrow{OL}=q$. The lengths satisfy $ED:DL=1:10$.\n\nExpress $\\overrightarrow{OD}$ in terms of $p$ and $q$. Fill in both coefficients, including their signs.\n\n$\\overrightarrow{OD}=$ {{field-1}} $p+$ {{field-2}} $q$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First express both endpoint vectors in the directions away from $O$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{OE}=p\\qquad \\overrightarrow{OL}=q .\n$$\n\nTrace the path from $E$ through $O$ to $L$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{EL}=\\overrightarrow{EO}+\\overrightarrow{OL}=-p+q.\n$$\n\nThe ratio $ED:DL=1:10$ gives $11$ parts in the whole segment. Thus\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{ED}=\\frac{1}{11}\\overrightarrow{EL}=\\frac{1}{11}(-p+q).\n$$\n\nAdd along the path $O\\to E\\to D$ and collect coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overrightarrow{OD}&=\\overrightarrow{OE}+\\overrightarrow{ED}\\\\&=p+\\frac{1}{11}(-p+q)\\\\&=\\frac{10}{11}p+\\frac{1}{11}q.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
